Z||000021||88formula||01-30-2001||06:47 PM||||I don't think it’s the fuel pump. If it was good before than chances are it is good now. The 3.1 and your 2.8-liter engines both run with the same fuel pressure so your stock fuel pump should run this motor fine. <P>What you need to do is get your mechanic to put a scanner on the engine and tell us what the BLM and INT numbers are. With those numbers and the other information we would be able to give you more accurate advice. It’s hard to diagnose an engine over the Internet with limited information and a motor that never came with the car in there. It could be a million different things that are causing your symptoms. <P><BR>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG">  <p>[This message has been edited by 88formula (edited 01-30-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000022||ironhedno3||01-30-2001||07:10 PM||||what year beretta was the engine out of?did you use the computer from the beretta or the fiero box..and how many miles are on the engine?stalling when its put in gear?has anyone looked for a vacuum leak?it would have to be a major leak if it wont get above 20 mph..stopped up cat? ||||reg||1
Z||000023||ThatRickGuy||01-31-2001||12:58 PM||||I'm not too familiar with the TDC 3.1, but it sounds like timing to me. if it has them, check the vaccum and mechanical advance. if it runs fine in neutral, but then dogs at the line, that would make me think it's not advancing the spark curve. make sure the mechanical advance. Other then that, look for vaccum leaks, any thing loose haning arround will most likely have a negative effect.||||reg||1
